# T0078 — Task Group nav sub-lists

**Task:** T0078 · id `90` · Ready · High · project 4 (TaskMesh)  
**Parent:** T0075 (id `87`, Pending) — first slice shipped (`0.23.0`); children remain  
**Depends on:** T0075 (`pending` — allowed)  
**Branch (after approval):** `T0078-task-group-nav`

**Out of scope:** T0077 auto-tag · T0079 Tags/Project filter fields · T0080 Project Phase field

## Goal

Let the user **opt a Task Group into the Project Menu** (middle pane) as a **sub-item under Tasks**. Selecting that item opens a **list view** of project tasks with the Group’s saved filter already applied.

Example labels the user might pin: Completed Tasks, On-hold Tasks, Draft State, Urgent Tasks. (Tags-based examples wait on T0079.)

## Decisions (confirmed)

| # | Decision |
|---|----------|
| A | **Opt-in** checkbox at the **bottom** of the Group edit modal: “Show under Tasks in Project menu”. Default **off**. |
| B | Persist `show_in_nav` on the **group row** (not localStorage). |
| C | Sub-items are **always visible** (indented under Tasks). No collapse/expand in v1. |
| D | Order follows the Group’s existing **sort order** among pinned groups only. |
| E | URL: `/projects/:id?tab=tasks&group=<groupId>`. Parent **Tasks** stays `/projects/:id?tab=tasks` (no `group`). |
| F | Clicking a sub-item opens a **flat List View**: only tasks matching the Group’s saved filter, **no Group/Unassigned header bars**, no Add group. Do **not** write into the main list’s localStorage while the `group` param is set. Editing/applying/clearing the list filter bar takes over: persist to localStorage and drop `group` (returns to the grouped board). Clicking **Tasks** restores the grouped board. |
| G | If the Group has **no active filter**, the checkbox is disabled (hint: save a filter first). On save with an empty filter, force `showInNav` false. Pinned groups whose filter is later cleared **drop out of the menu**. |
| H | Active highlight: the **sub-item** is active when `group` matches; **Tasks** is active only when `tab=tasks` and **no** `group` param. |
| I | Nav label = Group **name**. Optional **color** as a small swatch on the glyph, not the full row. |
| J | Switching away from Tasks **drops** `group`. Opening a task modal keeps `group` in the URL. |

## Scope

**In**

- Schema: `task_groups.show_in_nav` boolean, default `false`
- API: create/update/list include `showInNav`
- Group edit modal: checkbox + short hint
- `useShellNav` / `ContextNav`: nested children under Tasks; fetch project groups when on a project
- `ProjectDetailPage`: `group` query param → grouped `TaskBoard` with that Group’s filter as the list filter overlay
- Docs: `docs/database/projects-and-ideas.md` (and overview if the column list is mirrored); `npm run docs:sync-schema`

**Out**

- Auto-tag, extra filter fields, Project Phase field
- Pinning Unassigned
- Global `/tasks` menu (All Tasks / Unassigned) — this is **Project Menu** only
- Drag-reorder of nav items separate from Group reorder
- Persist focused-view filter edits back onto the Group (filter edits stay in the Group modal)

## Approach

### Schema (MINOR on finish-up)

1. Add `show_in_nav boolean not null default false` to `task_groups`.
2. Drizzle `schema.ts`, generate SQL, update `docs/database/`, `npm run docs:sync-schema`.

Existing groups stay unpinned.

### API

- `POST` / `PATCH` `/api/v1/projects/:projectId/groups` accept `showInNav` boolean.
- Empty-patch error message includes `showInNav`.
- GET project (or groups list) already returns full rows — clients pick up the field.

### Modal

- Checkbox bound to draft state; saved with name/color/filter.
- Disabled when the current filter draft is inactive (unless already saved-active and they’re only toggling pin before clearing — on save, pin + empty filter → `showInNav` stored but nav hides until filter exists; simpler: **on save**, if filter is null, force `showInNav` false).

### Project Menu

- Extend `ContextNavItem` with optional `indent` / `child` flag (or nested `children` on Tasks).
- Query `GET /api/v1/projects/:id/groups` (same key as the project page).
- Render pinned+filtered groups after Tasks, indented.
- Mobile: same list; keep touch targets.

### Grouped board + list filter overlay

- Parse `group` on `ProjectDetailPage` when `tab=tasks`.
- If id unknown / not in this project / no active filter: drop param.
- `listFilter` for the board and filter bar = that Group’s saved filter. Do not write localStorage until the user applies or clears the bar.
- Group sections behave as in T0075 (group filter overrides list filter).

