## QA follow-ups

- Group edit modal: nav checkbox sat **above** the label because `.field` is `flex-direction: column`. Replaced with a row layout so the checkbox sits to the left of “Show under Tasks in Project menu”.
- Duplicate `isFilterActive` import in `useShellNav.ts` caused a Vite parse error and blocked the Project menu from updating after pinning a Group. Removed the duplicate import; group PATCH now awaits query invalidation so the menu refreshes after Save.
- Nav sub-lists showed the filter bar correctly but still listed non-matching tasks because T0075 group filters **override** the list filter. **QA:** a sub-list is now a **flat** view: hide all Group/Unassigned bars, show only tasks that match the preset (including omitting non-matching children).
- Flat view still showed Group bars because `navListView` required the group row to be in memory and an effect **dropped `group` from the URL** when the overlay filter was not ready. Nav list mode is now **URL-driven** (`?group=`), that effect only removes unknown ids, and TaskBoard **never renders group header rows** in that mode (also de-dupes and re-filters tasks in the render path).
- DEV Vite was still transforming a **stale TaskBoard.tsx** (no `navListView` in the served module) while ProjectDetailPage had already updated — so the UI could not pick up list-view changes. Restarted Vite; enabled `server.watch.usePolling` so editor writes invalidate HMR.
